; ABNF mirror (descriptive, not test-parsed — the real byte-level walker is
; ../📡️component.protocol.semio, walked by dsl::walk_protocol) for s.stdio.semio.image snapshot
; (binary) — the shared `.semio` binary envelope (store::semio_format::wrap_binary) wrapping the
; REAL varint-length-prefixed SemioImageSnapshot binary pack (NOT serde_json::to_vec).
document        = envelope-magic token-len token format schema-len schema-bytes width height colorspace bit-depth payload
envelope-magic  = %x89 %x53 %x45 %x4D %x0D %x0A %x1A %x0A   ; 8 bytes: 0x89 "SEM" CR LF SUB LF
token-len       = 4OCTET                                     ; u32, little-endian
token           = 26OCTET                                    ; UTF-8 "s.stdio.semio.image.pack v1"
format          = OCTET                                      ; PACK_BINARY_FORMAT, currently 1
schema-len      = 1*OCTET                                    ; LEB128 varint
schema-bytes    = *OCTET                                     ; UTF-8 schema id, e.g. s.stdio.semio.image
width           = 4OCTET                                     ; u32, little-endian
height          = 4OCTET                                     ; u32, little-endian
colorspace      = OCTET                                      ; 0=Rgb 1=Rgba 2=Grayscale 3=GrayscaleAlpha 4=Indexed
bit-depth       = OCTET
payload         = *OCTET                                     ; icc/frames/metadata — see ../../🦀️component.rs's encode_image_snapshot_binary; opaque here (protocol-array-of-records gap)
